# GitLab2EdTechRAG - the CI-side counterpart of the /api/gitlab endpoints:
# it turns one pipeline run into POST /pull -> /chunk -> /embed for the commit
# range that pipeline covers.
#
# In production none of this is a file: the first two variables belong in the
# mirror repository's GitLab CI/CD variables (masked, protected), and the CI_*
# ones GitLab sets by itself. This file exists for a local dry run, where the
# CI_* values have to be faked:
#
#   cd /path/to/the/checkout
#   set -a && . /path/to/GitLab2EdTechRAG/.env && set +a
#   go run /path/to/GitLab2EdTechRAG/main.go
#
# git runs in the CURRENT directory, not in a configured workdir - so run it
# from the checkout whose commits the SHAs below refer to.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- own variables

# Base of the ingest API, WITHOUT /pull, /chunk or /embed - the tool appends
# those itself, in that order.
GitLab2EdTechRAG_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:5173/edtechrag/api/gitlab

# Shared secret of the EdTechRAG repository row: updateConfig has it under this
# exact key (Admin > Repositories > the repository > GitLab). Signs the body as
# X-Signature: sha256=<hmac>.
#
# This is the authentication, not optional hardening: in
# sveltekit/src/lib/server/gitlabApi.ts the check reads
# `if (signatureSecret && ...)`, so a row WITHOUT a stored secret accepts any
# request that carries some X-Signature header. The tool refuses to run without
# it.
GitLab2EdTechRAG_SHARED_SECRET=change-me

# ------------------------------------------------- GitLab's own CI variables
# Predefined in every pipeline. Set them by hand only for a dry run.

# The repository. MUST match updateConfig.repository_path of the EdTechRAG row
# EXACTLY - otherwise /pull answers 404 "Repository not found". Required.
# CI_PROJECT_PATH=llt/example-website-md

# The commit to index. In a pipeline this is the one that was just pushed. Any
# revision git understands works here - for a dry run, HEAD is fine. The value
# is only passed through and stored as meta.headSha on the DataFile rows; the
# file contents themselves are fetched by /chunk from gitlab_api_url + ref of
# the repository row, not from this SHA.
# CI_COMMIT_SHA=HEAD

# The commit the current index reflects; the diff CI_COMMIT_BEFORE_SHA..CI_COMMIT_SHA
# is what gets sent. Empty or all-zero (GitLab's value for a new branch) means
# "compare against the empty tree", i.e. send every file - that is the way to
# force a full re-index.
# CI_COMMIT_BEFORE_SHA=

# Only passed through to the API as "pipeline_source", for the log there.
# CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE=push
